## Overview

Four kernel wrappers on the MiniMax-M3 / NVFP4 / MXFP8 path repeat host work on every call that depends only on the layer, the device or the problem shape. This PR removes that work:

- the FlashInfer CUTLASS / CuTe-DSL MXFP8 linear kernels pass `skip_check=True` to `mm_mxfp8`;
- the MiniMax-M3 NVFP4 MSA impl builds its KV cache views once per layer;
- the TRT-LLM NVFP4 MoE passes `hidden_states_scale_layout` explicitly;
- the SM100 BF16x3 router GEMM caches its SM count and tile config.

